<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK FINMIN SETS ONE-YR BOND AUCTION FOR OCT 15.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK FINMIN SETS ONE-YR BOND AUCTION FOR OCT 15.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak Finance Ministry will auction an unspecified tranche of one-year bonds on October 15, the central bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the bonds, which will carry a 9.0 percent coupon paid semi-annually, will have a minimum price of par.</p>
<p>The bonds will hold a nominal value of 100,000 crowns, the central bank added.</p>
<p>In the last auction of similar bonds on September 24, in which all bids were rejected, the coupon was set at 8.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3687</p>
</text>
